the-firm-as-one-program-7 : List Word
the-firm-as-one-program-7 = unlines (cons "- **O4** Collaborative intelligence, information interactions, variance of expertise, choice of tool and focus of problem space lead to the unique choices of Citadel Securities and Jane Street: CitSec's C++ platform, Jane Street's OCaml platform." (cons "  - **O4.1** Jane Street: OCaml, chosen for correctness that a large group reviewing one another's code can rely on." (cons (quoted (cons "    - **O4.1.1** " (cons "Make illegal states unrepresentable" (cons " (Yaron Minsky): correctness is a property of the code everyone reads, not of the people who wrote it." nil)))) (cons "    - **O4.1.2** Pushed into everything: Async and Core libraries, HardCaml for FPGA design, and OxCaml (unboxed types, stack allocation, modes)." (cons "    - **O4.1.3** A firm built on correctness, reaching for control of the machine." (cons "  - **O4.2** Citadel Securities: C++, chosen for total control over layout, allocation and latency." (cons "    - **O4.2.1** Templates as a compile-time language for specialization. See [P5: Specialization (the Futamura projections) that keeps its proofs (hyperactivity v31 §6)], [C4: The fast path is a specialization that carries its proof ([P5], [P7])]." (cons "    - **O4.2.2** No proofs and pervasive undefined behaviour, so correctness rests on conventions, tests and review discipline." (cons "    - **O4.2.3** A firm built on control, reaching for correctness." (cons "  - **O4.3** Each firm bet on one half of the problem and now spends heavily to recover the other half." nil))))))))))
